1. Homepage
Purpose: Introduce your brand, build trust immediately, and guide visitors to services or consultation.
Sections:
	• Hero: “Modern Websites & Reliable Tech Support for Hill Country Businesses”
	• Sub‑headline: “Enterprise‑grade expertise with small‑town service.”
	• Primary CTAs: “Get Started” and “View Services”
	• Quick intro about you (with photo)
	• Services snapshot (Websites, Managed IT, Consulting)
	• “Why Choose Us” section
	• Testimonials (add later)
	• Service area map or list
	• Final CTA: “Schedule a Free Consultation”
2. About
Purpose: Build trust by showcasing your background, values, and local roots.
Sections:
	• Your story (Microsoft → Rackspace → Hill Country Web Works)
	• Mission, vision, and values
	• What makes you different (communication, reliability, enterprise skill)
	• Your approach: simple, friendly, clear
	• Photo(s) of you or local Hill Country imagery
3. Services (Overview Page)
Purpose: Provide a clear, simple overview of everything you offer.
Sections:
	• Intro paragraph: “Websites + Tech Support in One Place”
	• Three service categories:
		○ Website Design & Hosting
		○ Managed IT Support
		○ Cloud & Technical Consulting
	• CTA: “View Detailed Services” or “Schedule a Consultation”
4. Website Design & Hosting (Detailed Page)
Purpose: Sell your web services clearly and simply.
Sections:
	• What’s included in a website build
	• Examples of industries you serve
	• Hosting & maintenance details
	• Security & performance features
	• Pricing ranges
	• Process overview (Discovery → Build → Launch → Support)
	• CTA: “Start Your Website Project”
5. Managed IT Support (Detailed Page)
Purpose: Explain your moderate managed IT services in a way small businesses understand.
Sections:
	• What Managed IT means (in plain English)
	• Support tiers (Bronze, Silver, Gold)
	• What’s included:
		○ Backups
		○ Monitoring
		○ Troubleshooting
		○ Cloud/email fixes
		○ Light device support
	• Why small businesses need this
	• Pricing ranges
	• CTA: “Get Support for Your Business”
6. Cloud & Technical Consulting (Detailed Page)
Purpose: Highlight your advanced skills without overwhelming non‑technical clients.
Sections:
	• Azure/AWS setup and troubleshooting
	• Linux server expertise
	• DNS/email fixes
	• Performance tuning
	• Emergency troubleshooting
	• Security best practices
	• CTA: “Book a Technical Consultation”
7. Pricing
Purpose: Provide transparency and build trust.
Sections:
	• Website pricing tiers
	• Managed IT retainers
	• Hourly rates
	• Emergency rates
	• “Every project includes clear communication and documentation.”
